{
  "_about": "Dataset registry for data/dataset_0921: the single source of evaluation protocol and literature reference values. Runners read it by dataset name; do not override these fields per run. Values are fractions (0.9008 = 90.08%). Source of every SOTA number: docs/literature_sota_dataset_0921.md.",
  "_policy": {
    "role": "'report' datasets are where SOTA claims are made; system settings must be frozen before running them and may not be chosen by looking at their results. 'dev' datasets are for tuning and mechanism experiments.",
    "comparable": "true = same data version and protocol as the cited literature, numbers may be put side by side. false = report only, never claim SOTA; comparability_note says what is missing.",
    "gt": "null = no ground truth (detection fields are null); 'sibling' = <stem>_drift_times.txt next to each CSV, intervals [[start, end], ...] in output-row coordinates; 'generator' = produced with the stream.",
    "generator": "Stream generated in memory from a deterministic seed (no CSV on disk) with the listed injection parameters; one run per method x abruptness x trial.",
    "coordinates": "'input' = alarms, drift points and stream length counted in input rows, including rows the injection dropped (Cerqueira et al.'s convention). Default: rows the system saw.",
    "detect_from_fraction": "Alarms before int(fraction * n_input) + 1 are ignored by the evaluator (Cerqueira et al. do not feed the detector in the first 25%).",
    "comparable_kinds": "If set, only presets of these kinds produce comparable rows (others follow a different protocol).",
    "delta_max": "Cerqueira et al. maximum detection delay; the evaluator scores alarms in [d_s, d_s + delta_max] (their code) and also [d_s, d_e + delta_max] (their paper text)."
  },
